00:19:21.000 --> 00:19:59.000
So that part of it is an important first step. After that, it requires a trained mental health practitioner to then ask some important follow-up questions because a self-report questionnaire alone is really not enough, but we need to really know more about the setting, conditions under which this occurs, the degree to which it interferes with one's life. I mean, OMA's story is really quite intense in its conveys. about how much it can debilitate one. But also, her story is not uncommon in that many people who suffer it for so long are unaware that, wow, this is like, I don't have to live this way.

